<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss 1996 arms exports rise to 232.9 mln francs.</title>
<headline>Swiss 1996 arms exports rise to 232.9 mln francs.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's worldwide arms and weapons exports rose to 232.9 million Swiss francs in 1996 from 141.2 million in 1995, according to data released by the Swiss Federal Military Department.</p>
<p>Oman led the list of recipient countries, with imports totaling 65.4 million francs.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the department said Oman's order reflected a large order for air defence gun systems.</p>
<p>Germany was second on the list with orders totaling 33.8 million and the U.S. third with orders of 27.7 million.</p>
<p>In 1995, Germany imported 41.9 million of goods, and the U.S. imported 11.6 million. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
